# Rust build artifacts
target/
build/
build-w2/
dist/

# Cargo config (local build paths)
game/engine/.cargo/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local Claude Code session state
.claude/

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.venv/
*.log
__pycache__/
.superpowers/

# Three-site split — runtime files in each site's data dir.
# whitelist.txt and feedback-admins.json are intentionally tracked;
# *.log, *.key and .venv are caught globally above. This catches the
# admin-queue request log which doesn't match those patterns.
tools/sites/*/data/access-requests.jsonl
# Deprecated unified site — removed from the tree 2026-09-04; local leftovers (.venv, certs, data) stay ignored.
tools/website/
# Owner-only competitive-analysis dashboard — local tool, never tracked.
tools/feature-audit/
# Generated per-build by `cargo about` (native-packages.yml / build-local.sh) —
# must land here (not tools/packaging/staging/) for packager.toml's `resources`
# to find it; never hand-edited or committed.
/tools/packaging/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt


# Sensitive files
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
# Nostr secret keys — the canonical AxeNStax identity secret lives OUTSIDE the
# repo (~/.config/axenstax/). These patterns are belt-and-suspenders so a
# stray secret file dropped inside the repo can never be committed.
*.nsec
*.secret
/.secrets/
**/secrets/
*-official.json
credentials.json
serviceAccountKey.json

# Playwright MCP session dumps (console logs, page snapshots)
.playwright-mcp/

# Running the engine writes its per-install profile to `profile/` RELATIVE TO
# THE WORKING DIRECTORY: the Signet session, the runtime key, the mailbox key
# and the contacts mirror. All of it is private to one machine and some of it
# is secret — it must never be committed. Both spellings are needed: a run from
# the repo root, and a run from the crate directory.
/profile/
game/engine/profile/
